## Developer workflow

The repository uses `workflow_profile={{ workflow_profile }}`, `harness_mode={{ harness_mode }}`, `scm_provider={{ scm_provider }}`, `protected_main={{ protected_main }}`, `publish_mode={{ publish_mode }}` and `pr_merge_mode={{ pr_merge_mode }}`. Shared lifecycle scripts are versioned in this repository and updated through reviewed Copier releases.

For normal agent work:

```bash
python3 scripts/agent_doctor.py
python3 scripts/start_task.py my-task --task "OpenSpec add-x: 1-3" --scope "backend/..."
python3 scripts/select_checks.py --execute
python3 scripts/finish_task.py
python3 scripts/finish_task.py --status
```

`finish_task.py` enforces OpenSpec lifecycle hygiene and re-fetches `origin/{{ main_branch }}` immediately before publication. The core lifecycle pushes a verified feature branch and creates or reuses the selected provider's review object. GitHub preserves exact-head PR/check safety; GitLab observes the matching MR and CI status, then stops for human acceptance in the bounded standard adapter. Failed checks or merge leave local main unchanged. It never force-pushes, bypasses required checks, or auto-resolves divergence.

Platform-owned PR publication requires authenticated GitHub CLI/API access; run `gh auth login` once on the agent host or provide a supported `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN`. `agent_doctor.py` catches missing auth and invalid `protected_main=true + publish_mode=direct` before publication.

Platform-managed CI is self-contained in this repository and updates only through reviewed Copier releases; it does not execute `dev-platform@main` or require private cross-repository workflow access.

## Local and cloud verification

Required selected and full checks run locally before publication. Cloud CI is the clean-environment final gate for `publish_mode=pr`, and automatic task PR merge waits for it. Superseded validation runs are cancelled. Manual workflow dispatch is the explicit path when a full cloud run is useful.

For deliberately unprotected `publish_mode=direct`, the published main state receives an automatic run that is deliberately lightweight and validates platform/OpenSpec health without repeating the full project check set. Direct-mode repositories also keep the stable pull-request `platform-ci` compatibility gate for reviewed maintenance/rollout PRs.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/engineering/`.
